"""
MDAP/MAKER Complete Implementation

This module provides a complete implementation of the MAKER (Maximal Agentic decomposition,
first-to-ahead-by-K Error correction, and Red-flagging) framework as described in the paper
"Solving a Million-Step LLM Task with Zero Errors" (arXiv:2511.09030).

Key Features:
1. Algorithm 1: generate_solution - Main orchestration with voting
2. Algorithm 2: do_voting - First-to-ahead-by-k voting mechanism
3. Algorithm 3: get_vote - Voting with red-flagging
4. Algorithm 4: Recursive multi-agent solve with decomposition

This implementation provides:
- General-purpose decomposition (not just Towers of Hanoi)
- Four agent types: Decomposition, Decomposition Discriminator, Solution Discriminator, Problem Solver
- Recursive task decomposition with voting at each level
- Integration with existing MDAP infrastructure
"""

